  "post": {
    "caption": "This gem is fossilized wood. Whitby jet formed about 180 million years ago, in the Jurassic, and some say the trees were relatives of the monkey puzzle. The best known source is the coast near Whitby, England. Jet is light and feels warm to the touch, it is soft yet takes a high polish, and rubbed with wool it can build up an electric charge. Jet has been found in Bronze Age burial sites in Britain. Queen Victoria wore it in mourning after Prince Albert died in 1861, and by the early 1870s about 1,500 people worked in Whitby's jet trade. Imitation jet was often black glass, sometimes called French jet.",
